findings.body:
The `From<tray_icon::MouseButtonState>` impl maps `Up` to `MouseButtonState::Down` and `Down` to `MouseButtonState::Up`. The original code mapped them one-to-one, and nothing in the clippy fix calls for a change here. Every tray click that the native layer reports as released will now surface to Rust and JS listeners as pressed, and vice versa. No test exercises this conversion, so the existing serialization test (which hard-codes `MouseButtonState::Down` on its own value) will not catch it.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/tray/mod.rs" lines="30-38"}

Restore the one-to-one mapping. Consider adding a unit test that converts each `tray_icon` state and asserts the matching Tauri variant so this can't regress silently.

The original `#[cfg(feature = "isolation")]` applied only to the `impl Default for IsolationSide` block. The PR removes that impl and leaves the attribute in place, so it now attaches to the `#[derive(Template)] pub(crate) struct PatternJavascript` that follows. `crates/tauri/src/manager/webview.rs` imports `PatternJavascript` at line 25 and constructs it at line 131 with no cfg guard. Building `tauri` without the `isolation` feature will fail with an unresolved-name error.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/pattern.rs" lines="66-82"}

Remove the stray `#[cfg(feature = "isolation")]` that now sits directly above `#[derive(Template)]` and keep the gate on `IsolationSide` only, or check whether `PatternJavascript` should be gated at all. The `render_default` call in `webview.rs` needs it unconditionally.

The clippy `derive(Default)` cleanup has no need for a new constructor. `new_click` adds a new `pub fn` on the public `TrayIconEvent` type, and it is documented as a testing helper, which is a poor reason to widen a public API. It also hard-codes zeroed positions and sizes, which are not meaningful values for a real tray event. If tests need this, gate it behind `#[cfg(test)]` or `pub(crate)`, or move it into the test module that already exists in this file. Splitting it into its own PR with a changefile would also make the API change visible.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/tray/mod.rs" lines="136-155"}

If the helper is kept, it should be called out in `.changes` as a new public API, since the PR is otherwise a non-user-facing lint fix.

The `Up` variant is documented as `/// Mouse button pressed.` while `Down` is documented as released. This is pre-existing, but the PR touches the enum by adding `#[default]` to `Up` and it is the same line the inversion bug is on, so it is worth fixing while the reviewer is in this block. The doc text contradicts the variant name.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/tray/mod.rs" lines="21-28"}

Swap the two doc comments so `Up` reads as released and `Down` reads as pressed.
